---
import SplitSection from "../components/SplitSection.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import skate1 from "../assets/skate-1.png";
import skate2 from "../assets/skate-2.png";
import skate3 from "../assets/skate-3.png";
import skate4 from "../assets/skate-4.png";
import skate5 from "../assets/skate-5.png";
import skate6 from "../assets/skate-6.png";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Timer from "../assets/material-time.svg";
import Group from "../assets/material-group.svg";
---

<Layout>
  <Header />
  <SplitSection fullHeight={false}>
    <div slot="text">
      <h1>
        Skate Match is a mobile app that helps figure skaters find ice dancing
        or pair skating partners.”
      </h1>
      <div class="nested-container1">
        <div class="icon-column-s">
          <Image src={Timer} alt="diagnol arrow" />
        </div>
        <div class="body-column-s">
          <p>Ongoing, but so far 1 month</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="nested-container2">
        <div class="icon-column-s">
          <Image src={Group} alt="diagnol arrow" />
        </div>
        <div class="body-column">
          <p>I'm taking the role of UX Designer and Developer</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div slot="image">
      <Image
        src={skate2}
        alt="an image of a mobile screen filtering potential skating partners"
        width={skate2.width}
        height={skate2.height}
        class="image"
      />
    </div>
  </SplitSection>
  <SplitSection fullHeight={false}>
    <div slot="text">
      <h1>What Prompted this project?</h1>
      <div class="nested-container1">
        <div class="body-column">
          <h2>There's no efficient way to find a skating partner</h2>
          <p>
            Current methods include promoting yourself on social media which
            only works if you have a large following, asking in Facebook groups,
            or relying on your coach to know someone.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="nested-container2">
        <div class="body-column">
          <h2>The idea</h2>
          <p>
            Create an app for the sole purpose of matching skating partners
            where you don’t need a large following, or have to know someone
            personally.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div slot="image">
      <Image
        src={skate1}
        alt="an image of a skater's instagram post searching for a skating partner"
        width={skate1.width}
        height={skate1.height}
        class="image"
      />
    </div>
  </SplitSection>
  <SplitSection fullHeight={false}>
    <div slot="text">
      <h1>Validating the app with the Skating community</h1>
      <div class="nested-container1">
        <div class="body-column">
          <h2>I created a Figma prototype to guage interest</h2>
          <p>
            I used UX Pilot to create wireframes and prototyped the app with
            videos in Figma. I posted it on my skating TikTok asking if my
            followers would find it useful or want to use it. I also shared it
            with my coach and the USFS organization. I received positive and
            negative feedback and some suggestions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div slot="image">
      <Image
        src={skate4}
        alt="two mobile screens from the early version of the app showing options to book from different activites other than ice skating"
        width={skate4.width}
        height={skate4.height}
        class="image"
      />
    </div>
  </SplitSection>
  <SplitSection fullHeight={false}>
    <div slot="text">
      <h1>Responding to suggestions and negative Feedback</h1>
      <div class="nested-container1">
        <div class="body-column">
          <h2>Negative Feedback</h2>
          <p>
            USFS told me they think the app would face problems gaining users
            because our sport is so niche. I reminded them that they are the
            official US organization for Figure skating who also has an
            international skater following, so if they promote the app on their
            social media then there will be no problem gaining users. They
            shared it with their marketing team and asked me to update them when
            I finish coding the app.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="nested-container2">
        <div class="body-column">
          <h2>Suggestions</h2>
          <p>
            My TikTok followers suggested I make it a swipe/dating style app
            because of the “Matching” aspect which aligned with my early
            wireframes, but I decided against this because the quantity of
            videos needed in each profile would not work with a swipe style app.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div slot="image">
      <Image
        src={skate5}
        alt="an early version of the app showing a dating style swip app for figure skating profiles"
        width={skate5.width}
        height={skate5.height}
        class="image"
      />
    </div>
  </SplitSection>
  <SplitSection fullHeight={false}>
    <div slot="text">
      <h1>I decided to build the app after receiving feedback</h1>
      <div class="nested-container1">
        <div class="body-column">
          <h2>For effeciiencey, I built the frontend with Bolt.new</h2>
          <p>
            Bolt.new was able to generate wireframes matching the UI of the one
            I created with UX Pilot, but it struggled with the backend, so I
            transferred the project to VS code.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="nested-container2">
        <div class="body-column">
          <h2>Backend and VS Code</h2>
          <p>
            VS code lets me have version control history and it doesn't change
            things that I don't want it to change like Bolt.new does. This is
            more efficient for the final steps of the projecgt.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div slot="image">
      <Image
        src={skate6}
        alt="two mobile screens showing the waiver to sign and a QR code once completed"
        width={skate6.width}
        height={skate6.height}
        class="image"
      />
    </div>
  </SplitSection>
  <SplitSection fullHeight={false}>
    <div slot="text">
      <h1>Current and Next Steps</h1>
      <div class="nested-container1">
        <div class="body-column">
          <h2>Finish Coding, test, and promote</h2>
          <p>
            Once I finish the backend, I'll deploy the app and test it with my
            TikTok followers as part of an unmoderated usability test. Then I'll
            iterate and share the finished app iwth USFS to promote it on their
            social media.
          </p>
          <button
            onclick="window.open('https://www.figma.com/proto/airnBsCh4u3jvqGJay24kV/Ice-Time?page-id=0%3A1&node-id=1-4&p=f&viewport=718%2C91%2C0.1&t=SaQPNZrGNxVt0RSH-1&scaling=scale-down&content-scaling=fixed&starting-point-node-id=1%3A4&show-proto-sidebar=1', '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer')"
          >
            Try the Prototype
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div slot="image">
      <iframe
        style="border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);"
        width="800"
        height="450"
        src="https://embed.figma.com/proto/airnBsCh4u3jvqGJay24kV/Ice-Time?page-id=0%3A1&node-id=1-4&p=f&viewport=718%2C91%2C0.1&scaling=scale-down&content-scaling=fixed&starting-point-node-id=1%3A4&show-proto-sidebar=1&embed-host=share"
        allowfullscreen></iframe>
    </div>
  </SplitSection>
</Layout>
<style>
  .standaloneimg {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1rem;
  }
  .image {
    height: 600px;
    width: auto;
  }
  .icon-column-s img {
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
  }
  iframe {
    display: block;
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .image {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
    }

    iframe {
      display: none;
    }
    Header {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column-reverse;
    }
  }
</style>
